{title: Opposed This}
{subtitle: Ezra 10:15; 10:1–5; 10:7–9; 10:16–17}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A very large assembly gathered around
Men women and children all in the crowd
Weeping bitterly before the house of God
Con[Bb]fessing our sins as the tears did [Dm]flow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Shecaniah spoke up from the Elam line
We have been unfaithful to God divine
Yet now there is hope for Israel still
Send a[Bb]way all [Gm]these women as [Dm]we will
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Only Jonathan and [C]Jahzeiah opposed [G]this
Mes[Dm]hullam and Shab[C]bethai stood with [G]his
They [Dm]trembled at the com[C]mand of our [G]Lord
Ac[Bb]cording to the [Gm]Law it was re[Dm]corded
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
A proclamation went out to Judah and Ben
Gather in Jerusalem within three days
Or forfeit your property and be excluded
The [Bb]leaders and [Gm]elders made this de[Dm]cree
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
On the [Bb]twentieth of the ninth month we [Dm]sat
In the [Bb]open square in the heavy [Dm]rain
[Bb]Trembling because of this matter so [Dm]grave
The [Bb]weight of [Gm]the covenant was [Dm]on us
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From the first of the tenth to the [C]first of the first [G]
We [Dm]finished dealing [C]with all the [G]men
Who [Dm]had married foreign [C]women in the [G]land
The work [Bb]of the commis[Gm]sion was done
{end_of_verse}

